# f1 = sumHoled. The element is read in front of the branch, and the front end hands it on as an argument of the branch itself: it comes into the join by the fork's own edge, beside
# the written 0 of the other way. It is followed to the sum there too, and the holder is asked in front of the loop for a list of numbers. The hole makes the sum NaN, the text joins.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Array<number>
# CHECK: = GetArrayElement {{*}} arrayStorage=Double level=Proven
# RUN(ANSWER): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# ANSWER: sumHoled NaN NaN
# ANSWER-NEXT: sumMixed 1.25901.250 2.25901.250
# ANSWER-NEXT: exited with 0
